prompt: Load the kdevkit skill (from ~/.claude/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md, ~/.kiro/steering/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md, or ~/.codex/skills/kdevkit/SKILL.md — whichever exists). This repo keeps operational context in a repo-root AGENTS.md and project knowledge in specs/project.md. A feature just added a new lint step run with the command `just lint`. Record this durable operational change in the right context layer. Make the file edits now in this repo. When done print [kdevkit] applies.
tools: claude,kiro,codex
--- setup ---
git init -q
mkdir -p specs
cat > AGENTS.md <<'MD'
# todo-cli — agent guide

## Build & test
- Build: `cargo build`
- Test: `cargo test`

## Style
Run `cargo fmt` before committing.
MD
cat > specs/project.md <<'MD'
# Project: todo-cli

## Mission
A small command-line to-do manager.

## Architecture
One Rust binary.

## Tech Stack
Rust.

## Layout
src/main.rs.

## Testing
Unit tests are load-bearing; commands live in AGENTS.md.

## Deployment
cargo install.
MD
git add -A && git commit -q -m "seed" || true
--- assert ---
set -e
# The operational command landed in AGENTS.md (the operational layer).
grep -qF 'just lint' AGENTS.md
# It was NOT duplicated into project.md (which holds knowledge, not commands).
test -z "$(grep -F 'just lint' specs/project.md || true)"
# AGENTS.md stays a lean, convention-clean file — no kdevkit scaffold
# leaked in (no six-section headers, no HTML-comment prompts, no logs).
test -z "$(grep -iE 'Session Log|Decision Log|Active initiatives|Feature Brief|Implementation Plan' AGENTS.md || true)"
test -z "$(grep -F '<!--' AGENTS.md || true)"
